{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1400 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "0cf9b9c0b6be616ebaaac97a3d2e5723c5aa1f5341bb09adff6bd6737709aa06" :edb/db-before-t 1399 :edb/db-after-t 1400 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534712 50 #inst "2026-10-08T04:49:57.164Z" 13194139534712 true] [17592186096379 1100 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=3 \\\\ y+z=2 \\\\ z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186096379 1100 "Solve the following system of equations:\n$x + y + z = 3; y + z = 2; z = 2$" 13194139534712 false] [17592186096379 1145 "The third equation states that $z=2$. Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(2)=2 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad y = 2-2 = 0\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $z=2$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(2)=3 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x = 3-2 = 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x = 1$, $y=0$, and $z = 2$. Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 1,0,2 \\rangle$." 13194139534712 false] [17592186096379 1145 "The third equation states that $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(2)=2 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\ty = 2-2 = 0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $z=2$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(2)=3\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx = 3-2 = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x = 1,$ $y=0,$ and $z = 2.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 1,0,2 \\rangle.$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186096380 1100 "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186096380 1100 "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534712 false] [17592186096380 1145 "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1$, $x_2$, and $x_3$. We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\nx_{1} + x_{2} - x_{3} = 1; x_{2} + x_{3} =-2; x_{3} = 5\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $x_3=5$. Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(5)=-2 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_2=-2-5=-7\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 5$ and $x_2 = -7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx_1+(-7)-(5) = 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_1 = 1 + 7 + 5 = 13\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 13$, $x_2=-7$, and $x_3 = 5$. Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 13,-7,5 \\rangle$." 13194139534712 false] [17592186096380 1145 "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{3}=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $x_3=5.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(5)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-5=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 5$ and $x_2 = -7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx_1+(-7)-(5) = 1\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = 1 + 7 + 5 = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 13,$ $x_2=-7,$ and $x_3 = 5.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 13,-7,5 \\rangle.$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186096381 1100 "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186096381 1100 "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534712 false] [17592186096381 1145 "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1$, $x_2$, and $x_3$. We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n2x_{1} + x_{2} - x_{3} = 0; x_{2} + x_{3} =-2; 3x_{3} = 3\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n3x_3=3 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_3=1\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(1)=-2 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_2=-2-1=-3\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 1$ and $x_2 = -3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x_1+(-3)-(1) = 0 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} (3 + 1) = 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 2$, $x_2=-3$, and $x_3 = 1$. Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 2,-3,1 \\rangle$." 13194139534712 false] [17592186096381 1145 "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 3{x}_{3}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n3x_3=3 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \n\tx_3=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(1)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-1=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 1$ and $x_2 = -3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x_1+(-3)-(1) = 0\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} (3 + 1) = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 2,$ $x_2=-3,$ and $x_3 = 1.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 2,-3,1 \\rangle.$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186096590 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304918 13194139534712 true] [17592186096590 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304925 13194139534712 true] [17592186096590 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304939 13194139534712 true] [17592186096590 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304946 13194139534712 true] [17592186096591 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304953 13194139534712 true] [17592186096591 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304960 13194139534712 true] [17592186096591 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304967 13194139534712 true] [17592186096591 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304981 13194139534712 true] [17592186096591 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304988 13194139534712 true] [17592186096592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304932 13194139534712 true] [17592186096592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304974 13194139534712 true] [17592186096592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304995 13194139534712 true] [17592186096592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186305002 13194139534712 true] [17592186096843 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534712 true] [17592186096843 1100 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y-z=10 \\\\  & y+5z=15 \\\\  & -z=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186096843 1100 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n${x + 2y - z = 10; y + 5z = 15; - z = 5$" 13194139534712 false] [17592186096843 1145 "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n-z=5\\,⟹\\,z=-5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+5(-5)=15\\,⟹\\,y=15+25=40.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-5$ and $y=40$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+2(40)-(-5)=10\\,⟹\\,x=10-80-5=-75.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-75,y=40$ and $z=-5.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-75,40,-5⟩.$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186097096 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534712 true] [17592186097096 1100 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n${x_{1} + x_{2} - x_{3} = 3; x_{2} - x_{3} = \\frac{1}{2}; x_{3} = 2$" 13194139534712 false] [17592186097096 1100 "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=3 \\\\  & {x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & {x}_{3}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186097096 1145 "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-(2)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}+2=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5}{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(\\frac{5}{2})-(2)=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3+2-\\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{2}$, ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5}{2}$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{5}{2},2⟩.$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304918 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304919 13194139534712 true] [17592186304918 1089 "q-10195" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304918 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534712 true] [17592186304918 1100 "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & y+z=1 \\\\  & z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304918 1113 #uuid "86f396e6-bece-557c-89fe-7bc8d07b01b1" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304918 1145 "The third equation states that  $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\ny+2=1\\,⟹\\,y=1-2=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=2$ and $y=-1$into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-1)+(2)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}-2+1=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, $y=-1$, and $z=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩.$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304920 13194139534712 true] [17592186304919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304921 13194139534712 true] [17592186304919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304922 13194139534712 true] [17592186304919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304923 13194139534712 true] [17592186304919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304924 13194139534712 true] [17592186304919 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534712 true] [17592186304919 1041 "selection" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304919 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304920 13194139534712 true] [17592186304919 1110 #uuid "be15f084-0468-539e-9586-3dcf21de9144" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304920 1034 "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304920 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304920 1111 #uuid "fc0a6eba-eb8b-58ec-8897-d0cf1febfe20" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304921 1034 "⟨\\frac{3}{2},1,2⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304921 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304921 1111 #uuid "ae09bc59-42cc-51aa-9db6-d093d23069fa" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304922 1034 "⟨-\\frac{3}{2},-1,2⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304922 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304922 1111 #uuid "bdfacfc6-c10d-5ce5-8763-0b7178d5f4fc" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304923 1034 "⟨\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304923 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304923 1111 #uuid "6f792197-a7a6-50d1-9961-b194c7b83e98" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304924 1034 "⟨-\\frac{3}{2},1,2⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304924 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304924 1111 #uuid "90eec126-71d1-5c9a-9cb6-21f58fa00483" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304925 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304926 13194139534712 true] [17592186304925 1089 "q-10199" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304925 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534712 true] [17592186304925 1100 "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y-z=3 \\\\  & y-z=2 \\\\  & z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304925 1113 #uuid "557245ad-45e9-56b6-9e4b-33daba094cce" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304925 1145 "The third equation states that $z=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-(1)=2\\,⟹\\,y=2+1=3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=1$ and $y=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx-(3)-(1)=3\\,⟹\\,x=3+4=7.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=7$,  $y=3$,  and $z=1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨7,3,1⟩.$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304927 13194139534712 true] [17592186304926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304928 13194139534712 true] [17592186304926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304929 13194139534712 true] [17592186304926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304930 13194139534712 true] [17592186304926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304931 13194139534712 true] [17592186304926 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534712 true] [17592186304926 1041 "selection" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304926 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304928 13194139534712 true] [17592186304926 1110 #uuid "cdb603b5-cfa3-51c1-a64d-0eaea53c68f2" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304927 1034 "⟨5,2,0⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304927 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304927 1111 #uuid "64e1c4fa-7964-539e-ba2f-0cbc349382a4" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304928 1034 "⟨7,3,1⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304928 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304928 1111 #uuid "368b36f4-17b6-51cf-a950-0dc99d21e7a6" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304929 1034 "⟨5,3,-1⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304929 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304929 1111 #uuid "0f772a7f-048a-537d-a117-892b331c647e" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304930 1034 "⟨7,-2,-1⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304930 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304930 1111 #uuid "95b97466-613f-5dad-a9cc-1df6ee9e20ac" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304931 1034 "⟨6,2,1⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304931 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304931 1111 #uuid "4d92fa0b-61ff-5cf6-b0a7-2b60b6c5a15f" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304932 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304933 13194139534712 true] [17592186304932 1089 "q-10203" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304932 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534712 true] [17592186304932 1100 "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304932 1113 #uuid "c7e4218f-47e8-518f-8a12-cc5cea874766" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304932 1145 "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-2y+z=8 \\\\  & y-z=-1 \\\\  & z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-0=-1\\,⟹\\,y=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=0$ and $y=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x-2(-1)+(0)=8\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{8-2}{2}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3$, $y=-1$, and $z=0.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨3,-1,0⟩.$" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304934 13194139534712 true] [17592186304933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304935 13194139534712 true] [17592186304933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304936 13194139534712 true] [17592186304933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304937 13194139534712 true] [17592186304933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304938 13194139534712 true] [17592186304933 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534712 true] [17592186304933 1041 "selection" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304933 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304934 13194139534712 true] [17592186304933 1110 #uuid "63515660-8cda-56ff-ae25-8ef09026bdd0" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304934 1034 "⟨3,-1,0⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304934 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304934 1111 #uuid "aa53efee-83ce-5308-9161-139ad9390047" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304935 1034 "⟨2,-2,0⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304935 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304935 1111 #uuid "aa116539-a226-5200-9cb2-c11a3659577b" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304936 1034 "⟨0,1,-8⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304936 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304936 1111 #uuid "4d4d3fa8-869f-5a4f-b976-dfd62a77f30d" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304937 1034 "⟨2,-1,0⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304937 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304937 1111 #uuid "cbf4b6b5-bc24-5f6d-b9f5-7ecf4966ace1" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304938 1034 "⟨0,-1,8⟩" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304938 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534712 true] [17592186304938 1111 #uuid "848de5e7-387e-5d76-a00a-a3a0e44658d8" 13194139534712 true] [17592186304939 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304940 13194139534712 true] [17592186304939 108